A||||24||84fierotrevor||What is double clutch ?||||1||
Z||000000||84fierotrevor||11-08-2001||01:01 AM||||I heard vin diesel say it in the fast and the furious that you have to double clutch if u wanna win any street races. exatcly how do you double clutch ?<BR>and whats granny shifting ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-08-2001||02:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>I heard vin diesel say it in the fast and the furious that you have to double clutch if u wanna win any street races. exatcly how do you double clutch ?<BR>and whats granny shifting ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Movie hyperbole...<BR>If I have a good tranny and shifter, I don't even use the clutch...<BR>Any ways, clutch out of gear release clutch, hit gas, engage clutch and slam into next gear...<BR>I heard of granny gear, also known as creeper gear, very low first gear...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||02:47 AM||||If you don't use your clutch in your car, you'll be picking up pieces of it someday.  Automobile trannys weren't made for floating.  <P>Double clutching is used for upshifting as well as downshifting.  Most big truck trannies aren't synchronized.<P>84fierotrevor--Don't worry about trying to double clutch.  Just shift normally.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-08-2001||07:16 AM||||Granny shifting is just slow easy shifting.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||11-08-2001||12:13 PM||||It's bad to shift without the clutch? At some speeds and the right RPM, I dont have to push in the clutch to upshift. I can just lightly push the car into the next gear. Same for downshifting, but then I have to rev it a bit in N or it grinds.<P>I was told as long as your not grinding the trannie will be fine.<P>Now im confused!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||11-08-2001||12:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>If you don't use your clutch in your car, you'll be picking up pieces of it someday.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Master_Sushi, I think what he's saying here is "Don't try this at home."  If you don't know what you're doing, don't do it.  <P>Yeah, clutchless shifting can be done and probably won't hurt anything if you do it right and don't grind.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pheagey||11-08-2001||01:09 PM||||Isn't a double clutch like what are in bike? Multiply pressure plate...?<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed: Status: destiny unknown.<BR>Broken down: 3 times<BR>Broken into: 2  times (w/i 2 days).<BR>Killed: '97 Civic LX Auto,<BR>Killed by: '93 Civic EX 5 speed,<BR>[link]Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html[/link] (B4 vandalism)||||reg||2
Z||000007||filthyscarecrow||11-08-2001||02:32 PM||||if yuo're double clutching the upshifts, you're a moron. i didn't see fast and furious, but didn't they just drag race? you would not EVER double clutch in a drag race, unless you want to lose, synchros or no synchros. <BR>the idea behind double clutching is to match the RPM between the input shaft and the output shaft in the gearbox. in a synchronized gearbox (which is what we all have) there are little clutches on the shafts that engage when you hold teh shifter against the gate for the next gear down (ie. 3rd to 2nd downshift) and they spin everything up to speed so it all engages smoothly. racing gearboxes don't have synchros, so you have to double clutch them. the sequence goes like this: in 3rd gear, depress clutch, move shifter to neutral, release clutch, blip throttle to accelerate input shaft so it is spinning as fast as output shaft, depress clutch, move shifter to 2nd gear, release clutch. the right foot blips the throttle while it is doing the braking. you have to release the clutch in neutral to connect the engine to the input shaft and then blip it to get it spinning faster (lower gear means engine is spinning faster, given equal speeds) and then you can shift down. race cars won't go into gear unless you do this (trust me, i've tried hehe...) <BR>there is no need to double clutch the upshifts though, because the input shaft is slowing down when you lift on the upshift. you don't want the shaft to speed up, you want it to slow down to engage the next higher gear. when i was at skippy barber (don't tell them this) i wasn't even using the clutch on the upshifts. just lift and shift. clunks right in. my shifts were about .2-.3 sec. if you can double clutch an upshift faster than that, you're a f uckin cyborg. <BR>  double clutching is really only used in road racing, or when pitting in oval racing and the reason is because you only double clutch when you're braking (something not too many drag racers do during the race). you also won't notice much help on a street car gearbox even durign braking because they're synchronized and it's not necessary. i doublel clutch when i'm driving just because i'm used to doing it, and it's the only to shift quickly from 2nd to 1st. yuo'll notice a hesitation going into 1st when the car's moving faster than 5 mph. if you double clutch the 2nd to 1st downshift, there is no hesitation becasue you're doing the synchronizer's job for them, faster than they can do it. the autocrossers can probably vouch for that. <BR>  i think the people who made fast &furious didn't bother to do any research into what the racing jargon actually means. never trust a movie to learn about anything...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||11-08-2001||02:39 PM||||Double-clutching was used on street cars back in the 40's and 50's. The old old manuals were like the racing trans scarecrow mentioned. All manual transmissions in cars today use synchro's. Double clutching isn't needed.||||reg||1
Z||000009||84fierotrevor||11-08-2001||03:15 PM||||Ok, so what's this about some guy i was talking to at a importshop was telling me<BR>that in order to street race u have to basicly rev the engine when the flagger drops his hands put it in gear and instead of shifiting up you put it in nuterul rev the engine way up, Then put it in the next gear so it sorta speed boosts you or somthing ?<BR>and repeat all the way up to the highest gear or untell the race is over.<BR>I don't think he knows what he was talking about. lol<BR>does that work ?<BR>and if so is that supposed to be double clutching ?||||reg||6
Z||000010||BN Boomer||11-08-2001||03:49 PM||||I can't think of a single modern car I've driven that needed to be double clutched upshifting OR downshifting. The only time I have ever had to double clutch is when driving big rigs or older pickups with non-synchro trannies.<P>I haven't seen The Fast And The Furious, but their use of double clutching sounds about as realistic as a 17 shot revolver. Be very skeptical of ANYTHING AND EVERYTHING that comes out of Hollywood. Everytime Hollywood addresses a subject I am even the least bit knowledgable about, I notice grevious errors and inaccuracies.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierospeeder||11-08-2001||04:09 PM||||fierotrevor,  i think he might be refering to a turbo charger.<P>I got a 87 tbird turbo at home.  Its an automatic, so i just floor it and the trans does the shifting and it stays at full boost.<P>On my car, when its in neutral.  If i rev the engine, my boost gauge will not indicate any boost pressure.   this is in my car, but boost will only work if theres a load on the engine, so i cant comment on any other car.<P>If this is true with all cars, that a load has to be present for the turbo to kick in, then the ricer guy is just wasting time on his shifts.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||11-08-2001||06:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>Ok, so what's this about some guy i was talking to at a importshop was telling me<BR>that in order to street race u have to basicly rev the engine when the flagger drops his hands put it in gear and instead of shifiting up you put it in nuterul rev the engine way up, Then put it in the next gear so it sorta speed boosts you or somthing ?<BR>and repeat all the way up to the highest gear or untell the race is over.<BR>I don't think he knows what he was talking about. lol<BR>does that work ?<BR>and if so is that supposed to be double clutching ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>in a manual that's essentially revving the engine up to it's peak torque range, and then dumping the clutch... on an automatic.. it's a neutral drop. you'll need a new tranny shortly after you try that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cheever3000||11-08-2001||06:51 PM||||Grab-n-go is much better than grab-n-letgo-n-grabagain.  When it comes to racing, you'll hear a whole lot from people who don't know what they're talking about trying to sound like they know some secret.  There's more fiction being told than fact.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||11-08-2001||07:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>Then put it in the next gear so it sorta speed boosts you or somthing ?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A much safer way to do this, is put in a new torque converter btw.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
